From 085866cb50045b07c36d6c2bd899ef66ec5e5c86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:43:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: warm transcript cache for
 @session-referenced sessions so first ref clicks paint from cache

An @session mention usually names an old session outside the prefetcher's
PER_GATEWAY window, so its first click waited on hub REST (paint:"rest",
1.5 s on 11-02). Ref chips/links now ask main to prefetch the key the click
would paint from (owner resolved like the click: resolveSessionRefOwner), on
render and on pointer-enter, via a fire-and-forget
hermes:transcript-cache:prefetch IPC. Main dedupes queued/in-flight keys,
skips a current cache (hub meta from the last pass, else MIN_REFETCH_MS),
shares the tick's per-gateway backoff, and runs at most 2 per gateway.
